# COMANCHE: MAXIMUM OVERKILL — the WATCHED run's caption (doc/mods.md §1, betriebsart `watched`).
#
# THE PROBLEM THIS SOLVES, measured by the director round: the cut knows what it is looking at
# (`director CUT shot=wreck subject=sam team=hostile`) and told nobody but the console. Everything here
# is a fact the CLIENT observed — the cast copy it hands the director, and the director's own cut. No
# sensor, no seat, no simulation object: a spectator is not a pilot and this deck cannot become one,
# because the only names it may use are the watch feed's.

hud watch
scale 2.0
color 0.82 0.92 1.00

# ---- who is flying, and where
text x 0 dx 6 y 0 dy 12 size 1.15 text title
text x 0 dx 6 y 0 dy 26 size 0.95 text mission
text x 1 dx -6 y 0 dy 12 align r size 1.15 fmt "FRIENDLY %2.0f    HOSTILE %2.0f" src friendly src2 hostile
text x 1 dx -6 y 0 dy 26 align r size 0.95 fmt "T+%4.0f" src watch_t

# ---- what the camera is on, and why
text x 0 dx 6 y 1 dy -30 size 1.9 text subject
text x 0 dx 6 y 1 dy -12 size 0.95 text subject_team
text x 0 dx 70 y 1 dy -12 size 0.95 text subject_kind
text x 1 dx -6 y 1 dy -12 align r size 0.95 text shot
text x 1 dx -6 y 1 dy -26 align r size 0.95 text "HELD" when held

# ---- and who has just stopped flying. The eight-second window is DECLARED here, not baked into the
# engine: a caption that never faded would report a kill from four minutes ago as news.
text x 0.5 y 1 dy -66 align c size 1.5 text event when event gate event_age_s hi 8
text x 0.5 y 1 dy -50 align c size 0.95 text "DESTROYED" when event gate event_age_s hi 8
